From dff1bd0439d955f0885b6a0efbf81530aa5f81e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:24:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] mptcp: adapt kcov handle to kcov_common_handle_id wrapper

The kcov remote-handle helpers were written when the common handle was a
bare u64. Upstream commit 5a13e296a3e32 ("kcov: refactor common handle ID
into kcov_common_handle_id") wrapped it in a zero-sized-without-CONFIG_KCOV
struct, changing kcov_common_handle() and kcov_remote_start_common() to take
that type. Change msk->kcov_handle to struct kcov_common_handle_id so the
capture and the start helper type-check against the current API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxTZMJNnZE5MDKnwFWizdX
---
 net/mptcp/protocol.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/protocol.h b/net/mptcp/protocol.h
index da7b1eb892d9f..064d448ea1811 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/protocol.h
+++ b/net/mptcp/protocol.h
@@ -402,7 +402,7 @@ struct mptcp_sock {
 	 * socket.  Zero when the creating task had no kcov remote coverage
 	 * enabled, in which case the receive-path annotations are no-ops.
 	 */
-	u64		kcov_handle;
+	struct kcov_common_handle_id kcov_handle;
 #endif
 };
 
